hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1024","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Qais Al-Madani told us, he said: I heard Zayd bin Aslam, h, and Al-Rabi’ bin Suleiman narrated to us, Shuaib narrated to us, meaning Ibn Al-Layth, Al-Layth narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, H, and Ya’qub bin Ibrahim narrated to us Al-Dawraqi, Yazid bin Harun told us, Al-Majishun Abdul-Aziz bin Abdullah bin Abi Salamah told us, Zayd bin Aslam told us, H Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Hisham, who is Ibn Saad, told me that Zayd bin Aslam told them, This is the hadith of Al-Rabi’, and it is the best context for the hadith, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “If one of you doubts about his prayer and does not know how many times he prayed: one, two, three, or four, let him complete what he doubted. Then he prostrates two prostrations while sitting, and if his prayer was incomplete, then he has completed it, and the two prostrations are to discourage Satan, even if he has completed For his prayer, the rak’ah and two prostrations are voluntary.”"
"1025","Al-Rabi’ praised him again from his book, and said: “Let him build upon what he is certain of, then prostrate two prostrations before the greeting.” Abu Musa, Al-Dawraqi, and Yunus said: If one of you doubts about his prayer and does not know whether he prayed three times or four, then he should pray one rak’ah and prostrate two prostrations. He accepted the greeting, then the rest of their conversation was like the conversation of spring. Abu Bakr said to us: In this report I have evidence that if the owner of the money is absent from him, he pays his zakat. He gave it to the people of Sahman as charity, intending that if his money was safe then it was his zakat, and if his money was spent then it was voluntary, then It was clear to him and it was true that his wealth was safe, and that his wealth which he gave to the people of Sahman as charity was permissible on his behalf in the zakat obligatory in His money is absent, since the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, permitted the praying person to perform this rak’ah that he prayed as one of two, if his prayer was Which he prayed three times, then this is the fourth rak’ah, which is obligatory for him, and if his prayer was complete, then this rak’ah is voluntary, so it is permissible. This rak’ah is an obligatory rak’ah, and he only prayed it as if it was an obligatory or voluntary rak’ah."
